=no to work and~~ Requires a compositor which supports it. As of this commit only KWin supports this protocol.\r\n\r\n~~Really not sure when libdecor actually sets the xdg_toplevel so with it enabled I couldn't get it to work but I can confirm that without libdecor on KWin this does work~~\r\n![Screenshot_20250603_195429](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/355f59b4-c7f4-4fe6-a5c0-d4fe22df56a1)\r\n\r\nWorks with project icons too\r\n![Screenshot_20250603_201132](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a8f9dee-a3c3-41c6-9b30-b8ecb2e949e5)\r\n\r\nAdding a name to the icon is for icon themes, if a system theme has an icon called \"godot\" it will be used instead of whatever godot actually submits in the buffer (I'm guessing a bit here, I don't know of an icon theme that themes godot so I haven't tested. That also means there's a bug where the running app will get themed like it's the godot editor but not sure what the icon name should be in that case)\r\n\r\nUPD 1: added libdecor=yes support","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":129